<%# Navbar ✨ Entry token badge.

    Sits ON the profile avatar's upper-left corner (components/_user_nav
    "Div 3"), NOT next to the wallet balance — the balance slot instead swaps its amount
    for the full "✨ Free Entry" label (see layouts/_navbar.html.erb). Visible
    when current_user has any unconsumed entry tokens (web2 token economy — see
    docs/UI_PATTERNS.md "Entry Tokens (Web2 flow)").

    It wears .legendary-badge — the house legendary treatment (a panned gradient,
    white rim, warm bloom), built like the engine's .level-badge-10 but in the
    app's own primary + warning instead of a fixed 8-stop rainbow — so a free
    entry reads as the prize it is. That class is PAINT ONLY; the w-5/h-5/
    rounded-full below are the geometry. Both live in
    app/assets/tailwind/application.css.

    Three affordances, all on the one 20px disc:
      hover/focus — reveals "✨ Free Entry" OVER the wallet balance, so a user
                    who doesn't recognise the sparkle gets the answer where
                    they were already looking. Driven by `freeEntryHover` in
                    the _user_nav Alpine scope (Alpine scope is DOM-based, so
                    the balance slot rendered into that same wrapper reads it).
      click       — opens the settings sidebar, exactly as the avatar and the
                    username beside it do. It used to pop its own 2-second
                    count popover; that made the badge the ONE control in this
                    cluster that went somewhere else, and the count now lives
                    in the sidebar the click opens (components/_gear_sidebar).
                    @click.stop is load-bearing — without it the same click
                    reaches the panel's @click.outside and shuts what it just
                    opened.
      level-up    — .free-entry-glow pulses the badge (armFreeEntryGlow in
                    solana_utils.js, fired from the layout's level-up listener).

    JS contract:
      [data-free-entry-badge]   — selector used by solana_utils.js for
                                  updateNavTokens / refreshBalance /
                                  animateFreeEntryBadge / glowFreeEntryBadge /
                                  fireConfettiFromBadge.
      .free-entry-badge         — CSS class for the .free-entry-punch
                                  animation triggered after a token-funded
                                  entry confirms.
      .free-entry-glow          — level-up glow pulse (3 beats, ~4.2s).
      data-token-count          — live token count; updateNavTokens()
                                  writes here so the popover reads the
                                  current value on each open instead of
                                  the server-rendered snapshot.
      .hidden                   — lives on the button (not the wrapper)
                                  so the JS selectors above can surface
                                  the badge after a mint without a reload.
                                  It HIDES as well now, which took an
                                  explicit rule rather than the bare class.
                                  .hidden and the inline-flex beside it are
                                  both single-class utilities in the same
                                  layer, so they tie and source order decides
                                  — Tailwind emits .hidden first, inline-flex
                                  won, and a zero-token user kept a live
                                  20x20 sparkle while updateNavTokens(0) sat
                                  inert. The compound, unlayered override
                                  that settles it lives beside .free-entry-
                                  badge in app/assets/tailwind/application.css,
                                  and the PAINT is measured in
                                  e2e/navbar_layout.spec.js. The bare class
                                  still settles nothing on its own, so do not
                                  carry this assumption to another element.
%>
<%# Cache-first count (display_entry_token_count): a warm cache renders the
    real count immediately; a COLD cache renders nil → the badge starts hidden
    ("loading") and refreshSession()'s updateNavTokens paints it once the
    hydrate lands — same loading→hydrated UX the balance pill already uses. The
    count is display-only; funding re-derives tokens live server-side. %>
<% free_entries = display_entry_token_count.to_i %>
<% plural_suffix = free_entries == 1 ? "" : "s" %>

<%# .free-entry-badge / .free-entry-punch / .free-entry-glow / .free-entry-label
    live in app/assets/tailwind/application.css. No x-data here any more — the
    popover took the count with it into the sidebar, and the hover writes to
    `freeEntryHover` in the _user_nav scope above, not to a scope of its own. %>
<div class="relative flex-shrink-0 leading-none">
  <button type="button"
          @click.stop="$store.sidebars.gearOpen = !$store.sidebars.gearOpen"
          @mouseenter="freeEntryHover = true"
          @mouseleave="freeEntryHover = false"
          @focus="freeEntryHover = true"
          @blur="freeEntryHover = false"
          title="<%= free_entries %> unconsumed entry token<%= plural_suffix %> — free entry"
          aria-label="<%= free_entries %> free entry token<%= plural_suffix %> — open settings"
          aria-controls="gear-sidebar gear-sidebar-mobile"
          aria-haspopup="dialog"
          :aria-expanded="$store.sidebars && $store.sidebars.gearOpen ? 'true' : 'false'"
          class="free-entry-badge legendary-badge inline-flex items-center justify-center w-5 h-5 rounded-full cursor-pointer <%= 'hidden' unless free_entries.positive? %>"
          data-free-entry-badge="true"
          data-token-count="<%= free_entries %>">
    <span aria-hidden="true" style="font-size: 12px; line-height: 1;">✨</span>
  </button>
</div>
